1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,761
A contact is the person you call or text.

2
00:00:03,761 --> 00:00:07,637
This video shows how a contact type is set up, how to create

3
00:00:07,637 --> 00:00:11,514
a contact, how to find one by name or phone number, what you

4
00:00:11,514 --> 00:00:15,860
can do from a contact, and what the import and export screens offer.

5
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:25,366
Every call, text and conversation needs to be tied to a person.

6
00:00:25,366 --> 00:00:31,480
Without that, an agent answers a caller as a stranger and asks everything again.

7
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:37,079
A contact keeps the person's name, their phone numbers and email addresses, their

8
00:00:37,079 --> 00:00:39,810
time zone, and what they agreed to receive.

9
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:45,591
Every activity, call and conversation links back to the contact, so the whole

10
00:00:45,591 --> 00:00:47,470
history is on one screen.

11
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:52,088
A contact is an ordinary content item of a type that has the

12
00:00:52,088 --> 00:00:55,780
Omnichannel Contact part, so you can add your own fields.

13
00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:03,645
An administrator sets the contact type up once.

14
00:01:03,645 --> 00:01:09,130
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit the Contact type.

15
00:01:09,583 --> 00:01:11,981
Edit the Omnichannel Contact part.

16
00:01:11,981 --> 00:01:17,137
Auto detect time zone works out the contact's time zone from their phone number.

17
00:01:17,137 --> 00:01:21,153
Require time zone makes it mandatory when auto detect is off.

18
00:01:21,625 --> 00:01:25,474
Use Do not call, Use Do not SMS and Use Do not email

19
00:01:25,474 --> 00:01:28,261
show each preference on the contact.

20
00:01:28,261 --> 00:01:30,915
Only Do not call is on by default.

21
00:01:31,368 --> 00:01:37,588
The part also adds the Contact Methods list, where phone numbers and email addresses are stored.

22
00:01:37,588 --> 00:01:42,648
Dialers, loads and imports always read numbers from it, so leave it in place.

23
00:01:46,886 --> 00:01:49,741
Open Interaction Center, Contacts.

24
00:01:49,741 --> 00:01:55,665
Each row is a contact, with buttons to list its activities, edit and view it.

25
00:01:55,665 --> 00:01:57,806
Click New, then Contact.

26
00:01:58,257 --> 00:02:01,746
Fill in the first and last name, and the job title.

27
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:06,277
The Account picker puts the contact in a company when the CRM is on.

28
00:02:06,733 --> 00:02:10,967
Under Contact Methods, click Add Item and choose Phone Number.

29
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:14,393
Type the number, and pick its type, such as Cell.

30
00:02:16,488 --> 00:02:21,347
Leave Contact time zone on Automatic to detect it from the number, or pick one.

31
00:02:21,347 --> 00:02:24,891
Tick Do not call when the person asked not to be called.

32
00:02:24,891 --> 00:02:27,578
Dialers and automated messages skip them.

33
00:02:28,044 --> 00:02:29,324
Click Publish.

34
00:02:29,324 --> 00:02:31,694
The new contact is on the list.

35
00:02:35,994 --> 00:02:41,139
On the Contacts list, the search box matches a name or a phone number.

36
00:02:41,139 --> 00:02:44,254
Type a name, such as Elena, to find her.

37
00:02:44,736 --> 00:02:48,899
Type three digits or more, such as seven zero two five five five,

38
00:02:48,899 --> 00:02:52,946
and the list shows contacts whose main number begins with them.

39
00:02:53,536 --> 00:02:55,788
Search terms are more precise.

40
00:02:55,788 --> 00:03:01,603
Phone matches digits anywhere, Phone Ends matches the last digits, Phone Starts matches

41
00:03:01,603 --> 00:03:06,981
the first digits, and Phone Exact matches the whole number however it was saved.

42
00:03:06,981 --> 00:03:11,796
The Filter syntax entry of the Filters menu shows them on a Phone card.

43
00:03:15,925 --> 00:03:17,531
Open a saved contact.

44
00:03:17,531 --> 00:03:20,265
The buttons at the top lead to its work.

45
00:03:22,204 --> 00:03:26,784
List Activities shows the contact's scheduled and completed activities.

46
00:03:27,296 --> 00:03:32,201
Add Activity, Outbound, schedules a call or message to the contact.

47
00:03:32,201 --> 00:03:37,376
Add Activity, Inbound, logs a call or message that the contact started.

48
00:03:41,676 --> 00:03:44,940
Contacts load from a file with Content, Import.

49
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:48,266
For a contact type the import page adds options:

50
00:03:48,266 --> 00:03:53,933
Ignore duplicate by phone number, Compare with, which records count as duplicates, and

51
00:03:53,933 --> 00:03:57,136
the Lead country that local numbers belong to.

52
00:03:57,706 --> 00:04:02,571
On the export page, a contact type shows a CRM last activity section.

53
00:04:02,571 --> 00:04:08,668
Tick Include last completed activity information, choose a Subject, and the file carries

54
00:04:08,668 --> 00:04:11,456
each contact's latest activity on it.

55
00:04:15,656 --> 00:04:20,026
Recognize a caller by their number, instead of treating them as a stranger.

56
00:04:20,776 --> 00:04:25,956
Respect each person's do-not-call, do-not-text and do-not-email choices.

57
00:04:26,706 --> 00:04:31,336
Call people at a sensible local time, using the contact's time zone.

58
00:04:32,086 --> 00:04:38,106
Load a list of contacts from a spreadsheet, and export them again with their latest activity.

59
00:04:40,106 --> 00:04:44,666
Set the contact type up once, and every call, text and conversation is

60
00:04:44,666 --> 00:04:46,046
tied to a person.

61
00:04:46,046 --> 00:04:49,826
Agents then see who is calling, when it is a good time to

62
00:04:49,826 --> 00:04:52,826
call, and what the person agreed to receive.

63
00:04:52,826 --> 00:04:54,386
Thanks for watching.

